{"html":"<p>A web server answers many requests at once. A report calls three slow services and could call them in parallel. Both need <strong>concurrency</strong>: several things in progress at the same time. Java has rich tools for it, and one rule above all: shared data needs protection.</p>\n<h2 id=\"threads\">Threads</h2>\n<p>A <strong>thread</strong> is a path of execution. Every program starts with one, the main thread; you can start more:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">Thread</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> thread</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Thread</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"hello from \"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> Thread.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">currentThread</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">().</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">getName</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">()));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">thread.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">start</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// runs in parallel</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">thread.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">join</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();    </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// wait for it to finish</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Call <code>start()</code>, not <code>run()</code>: <code>run()</code> would just execute the code in the current thread. In real code you&#39;ll rarely create threads by hand; executors (below) do it for you.</p>\n<h2 id=\"race-conditions\">Race Conditions</h2>\n<p>Two threads each add 1 to a shared counter, 100,000 times:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">static</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> int</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> count</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">Runnable</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> work</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> () </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    for</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> i</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; i </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 100_000</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; i</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">++</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        count</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">++</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">};</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Run it in two threads, and the result is usually <strong>less than 200,000</strong>. <code>count++</code> is really three steps: read, add, write. Two threads can read the same value, both add one, and both write it back: one increment is lost. That&#39;s a <strong>race condition</strong>, and it can hide for months, then corrupt data under load.</p>\n<h2 id=\"fixing-shared-state\">Fixing Shared State</h2>\n<h3 id=\"synchronized\">synchronized</h3>\n<p>Only one thread at a time can run a <code>synchronized</code> method on the same object (or class, for <code>static</code>):</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">static</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> synchronized</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> void</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> increment</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    count</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">++</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Correct, but threads wait for each other, so keep synchronized blocks short.</p>\n<h3 id=\"atomic-variables\">Atomic Variables</h3>\n<p>For a single counter or value, the atomic classes are faster and simpler:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">AtomicInteger</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> count</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> AtomicInteger</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">count.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">incrementAndGet</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// read, add and write as one step</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Both fixes give exactly 200,000.</p>\n<h3 id=\"concurrent-collections\">Concurrent Collections</h3>\n<p><code>HashMap</code> and <code>ArrayList</code> break when several threads change them. Use the concurrent versions:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">Map</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">String</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">, </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Integer</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">> </span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">counts</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> new</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> ConcurrentHashMap&#x3C;>();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">counts.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">merge</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"hits\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, Integer</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">::</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">sum);   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// safe from many threads</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><h3 id=\"or-share-nothing\">Or Share Nothing</h3>\n<p>The safest shared state is none. Immutable objects, like records, can be shared freely, because nobody can change them. Prefer passing data to tasks and getting results back over changing shared variables.</p>\n<h2 id=\"executors-and-futures\">Executors and Futures</h2>\n<p>Creating a thread per task is expensive and unbounded. An <strong>executor</strong> keeps a pool of threads and runs tasks on them:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">try</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (ExecutorService</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> pool</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> Executors.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">newFixedThreadPool</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">4</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">)) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    Future</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Integer</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">> </span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">future</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> pool.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">submit</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-></span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 6</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> *</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 7</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(future.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">get</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">());   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// waits, then prints 42</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><ul>\n<li><code>submit</code> returns a <strong>Future</strong> at once; <code>get()</code> waits for the result.</li>\n<li>Since Java 19, an executor is <code>AutoCloseable</code>: try-with-resources waits for the tasks and shuts it down.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>invokeAll</code> runs several tasks and waits for all of them. Three calls of 100 ms each take about <strong>100 ms in total</strong> instead of 300:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">List</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">Callable</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">String</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">>> </span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">tasks</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> List.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">of</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-></span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> fetch</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"a\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">), () </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-></span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> fetch</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"b\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">), () </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-></span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> fetch</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"c\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">for</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (Future</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">String</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">> </span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">result</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> :</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> pool.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">invokeAll</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(tasks)) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(result.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">get</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">());</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><h2 id=\"completablefuture-chaining-async-work\">CompletableFuture: Chaining Async Work</h2>\n<p><code>CompletableFuture</code> lets you describe steps that run when results arrive, and combine several:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">CompletableFuture</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">String</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">> </span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">summary</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> CompletableFuture.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">supplyAsync</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-></span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"price\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    .</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">thenApply</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(text </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> text </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \" 42\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    .</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">thenCombine</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(CompletableFuture.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">supplyAsync</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-></span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"stock 3\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">),</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">                 (price, stock) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> price </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \", \"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> stock);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">System.out.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">println</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(summary.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">get</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">());   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// price 42, stock 3</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Add <code>exceptionally</code> or <code>handle</code> to deal with failures, and <code>orTimeout</code> so nothing waits forever.</p>\n<h2 id=\"virtual-threads-java-21\">Virtual Threads (Java 21)</h2>\n<p>A classic platform thread maps to an operating system thread: each costs memory, and a server can run a few thousand. Most server threads spend their time <strong>waiting</strong> for a database or an HTTP call.</p>\n<p><strong>Virtual threads</strong> are lightweight threads managed by the JVM. When one waits on I/O, it steps aside and frees its carrier thread for others. You can run <strong>millions</strong> of them:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">try</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (ExecutorService</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> executor</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> Executors.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">()) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    for</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> i</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; i </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 10_000</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; i</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">++</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        executor.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">submit</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-></span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> fetch</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"task\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">));   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// each waits 100 ms</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 10,000 tasks finish in well under 2 seconds</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>You write plain, blocking code, one thread per task, and get the scalability of async code. Start one directly with <code>Thread.ofVirtual().start(task)</code>. In Spring Boot, <code>spring.threads.virtual.enabled=true</code> serves each request on a virtual thread.</p>\n<p>Virtual threads help with <strong>waiting</strong>, not with heavy <strong>computation</strong>: CPU-bound work still needs a pool sized to the number of cores.</p>\n<h2 id=\"common-pitfalls\">Common Pitfalls</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Unprotected shared state:</strong> any field changed by several threads needs synchronization, an atomic or a concurrent collection.</li>\n<li><strong>Deadlocks:</strong> thread 1 holds lock A and waits for B, thread 2 holds B and waits for A. Always take locks in the same order.</li>\n<li><strong>Blocking forever:</strong> use timeouts on <code>get</code> and on network calls.</li>\n<li><strong>Swallowed exceptions:</strong> an exception in a task is stored in its <code>Future</code> and only seen when you call <code>get()</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Thread-safe parts aren&#39;t a thread-safe whole:</strong> &quot;check, then act&quot; on a <code>ConcurrentHashMap</code> can still race; use atomic methods like <code>merge</code> and <code>computeIfAbsent</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"the-answer-in-short\">The Answer in Short</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Threads run code in parallel; prefer executors over creating threads yourself.</li>\n<li>Shared changing data causes race conditions: use <code>synchronized</code>, atomics or concurrent collections, or share nothing.</li>\n<li>Executors run tasks on a pool and return Futures; close them with try-with-resources.</li>\n<li><code>CompletableFuture</code> chains and combines async results; always handle errors and timeouts.</li>\n<li>Java 21&#39;s virtual threads make blocking code scale to millions of waiting tasks; they don&#39;t speed up computation.</li>\n</ol>\n"}